/*
Problem: Maximum Number of Vowels in a Substring
of Given Length
Platform: LeetCode (LC 1456)
Topic: Sliding Window (Fixed Size)

---------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

We need to find the maximum number of
vowels present in any substring of
length k.

Instead of checking every substring
independently (O(nk)),

maintain a sliding window of size k.

---------------------------------------------------------

Sliding Window Idea:

Maintain:

st   → left boundary

end  → right boundary

count

Number of vowels currently inside
the window.

---------------------------------------------------------

For every character:

If it is a vowel,

Increase count.

---------------------------------------------------------

If window size becomes greater than k:

Remove the leftmost character.

If it was a vowel,

Decrease count.

Move st forward.

---------------------------------------------------------

Whenever window size becomes exactly k:

Update:

maxVowels = max(maxVowels, count)

Continue sliding.

---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

s = "abciiidef"

k = 3

--------------------------------

Window:

"abc"

Vowels = 1

Answer = 1

--------------------------------

Slide

"bci"

Vowels = 1

--------------------------------

Slide

"cii"

Vowels = 2

Answer = 2

--------------------------------

Slide

"iii"

Vowels = 3

Answer = 3

Maximum = 3

---------------------------------------------------------

Why Sliding Window Works?

When moving the window by one position:

Only two characters change:

1. One enters.

2. One leaves.

So update the vowel count in O(1)
instead of recounting the entire window.

---------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity:

O(n)

Each character enters and leaves
the window at most once.

---------------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity:

O(1)

Only a few variables are used.

---------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int maxVowels(string s, int k) {

        int st = 0;
        int count = 0;
        int maxVowels = 0;

        for (int end = 0; end < s.length(); end++) {

            // Add current character
            if (s[end] == 'a' || s[end] == 'e' ||
                s[end] == 'i' || s[end] == 'o' ||
                s[end] == 'u') {

                count++;
            }

            // Shrink window if it exceeds size k
            while (end - st + 1 > k) {

                if (s[st] == 'a' || s[st] == 'e' ||
                    s[st] == 'i' || s[st] == 'o' ||
                    s[st] == 'u') {

                    count--;
                }

                st++;
            }

            // Window size is exactly k
            if (end - st + 1 == k) {

                maxVowels = max(maxVowels, count);
            }
        }

        return maxVowels;
    }
};
